const e="Easy Guide to Starting Online Therapy Sessions from Home | Michelle Barratt Psychology",t="When life feels messy or overwhelming, online therapy sessions are becoming a more common way for people to get support. They’re helpful when someone wants to",s='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/blog" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Blog</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">Easy Guide to Starting Online Therapy Sessions from Home</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">14 December 2025</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">Easy Guide to Starting Online Therapy Sessions from Home</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"><p>When life feels messy or overwhelming, online therapy sessions are becoming a more common way for people to get support. They’re helpful when someone wants to talk but doesn’t have the time or headspace to run across town. Around the holida</p></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/care-learning-9954699_1280.jpg" alt="" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">When life feels messy or overwhelming, online therapy sessions are becoming a more common way for people to get support. They’re helpful when someone wants to talk but doesn’t have the time or headspace to run across town.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Around the holidays, when things tend to pile up emotionally, we see more people turning to this option, especially couples and teenagers. Between school holidays, travel, and the general summer busyness, it’s comforting for many to be able to check in from home.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Starting something new can feel uncertain, and that’s normal. If therapy from home is something you’re thinking about, it might help to know what it actually looks like. A few small steps can make the whole thing less stressful, and sometimes just knowing what to expect makes it feel easier.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Why People Choose Therapy from Home</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">There’s something nice about staying in familiar surroundings when talking about things that can feel hard. That’s one of the biggest reasons people say they prefer online support over in-person sessions, especially during summer when routines shift and travel picks up.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>It saves time, sessions can fit more easily into a lunch break or a quiet evening without needing to drive across town.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>It feels private, no waiting rooms or running into someone you know. You can be sitting on your couch in comfy clothes with no pressure to tidy up for anyone.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>For couples, it can ease tension, being in a calm space makes it easier to talk through things without feeling like you’re on display.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Teenagers often find it less confronting, when they’re in a spot they know, they tend to open up quicker. School holidays can knock routines around, and for teens, not having to go somewhere new to talk can be a real plus.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>At Michelle Barratt Psychology, our online therapy services use secure video platforms, so your conversations are private and your data is protected.</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">These reasons don’t make online support better or worse than in-person, it just means that, for some people, it’s the option that makes the most sense right now.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Getting Set Up for an Online Session</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Starting online therapy doesn’t need to be complicated. Once the session is booked in, a few things can help make it run smoother.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>A phone, tablet, or laptop works well, as long as there’s a good internet connection.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Headphones can keep things private, especially if others are close by. For teens, this can help them feel more in control of who can hear what’s going on.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Find a spot where you won’t be interrupted. It doesn’t have to be perfect, just a space where you feel safe and held, even if that’s a bedroom or a chair on the back deck.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Let others in the house know when you’ll need space. It avoids knocks or walk-ins. For couples, giving one another time to get mentally ready can make a big difference too.</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Our psychologists are registered with the Psychology Board of Australia and have experience delivering telehealth and online therapy for a broad range of issues, including anxiety, relationship difficulties, and family conflict.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">What matters most is that the space feels safe, not fancy. It’s okay if the dog barks or if someone walks past outside. Life keeps happening around us, and that’s fine.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What Online Therapy Sessions Are Like</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Most online therapy sessions start a lot like in-person ones. There’s a check-in, a chance to talk through what’s been going on, and space to be listened to without judgement. For teens or couples who are new to it, the first session might just focus on getting comfortable and building trust.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Therapists are used to working with people through a screen. They know how to tune in and respond, even when the session isn’t face to face.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>For teens, they often give more space to speak up in their own way, which might include texting or writing things down during the session if that’s easier.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>For couples, therapy might include talking through habits, disagreements, or mismatched expectations. Online sessions let couples do this from a space that feels familiar, which can remove some of the pressure.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Sessions usually last under an hour and include pauses for reflection, clarifying what’s being said, and checking how each person is feeling.</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s okay to be unsure at first. Most people take a few sessions to get used to the flow. The main thing is showing up and being willing to give it a try.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Fitting Therapy into Your Summer Holidays</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">December in Australia comes with long days, school break, extra family time, and sometimes, extra stress. For many families, this is when emotions run high, especially for teenagers dealing with changes in friendships or couples sorting out holiday plans under the heat of summer and pressure to ‘make things perfect.’</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">This is why online therapy sessions often feel easier to fit in during this time of year.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>They can work around travel plans, if you’re away at a family beach house or staying with relatives, sessions can still go ahead.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>They don’t need you to cancel everything else, if the kids are off school, you’re taking time off work, or there are visitors staying over, there’s still space for support.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>They give you a quiet check-in point in a season that often runs on emotion and expectation.</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Having support that doesn’t get paused with the seasons can help things feel less heavy, especially when small issues start to feel bigger.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Finding Calm Without Leaving Home</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Online therapy sessions are one way people are grounding themselves during a full season. They offer flexibility, privacy, and a little more ease, especially for teenagers and couples whose needs can shift quickly based on what’s happening around them.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Whether it’s about ongoing challenges or just a feeling that things aren’t sitting right, having a space to talk from home can make all the difference. You don’t have to wait until things get too loud or too tangled. Sometimes the best kind of support is the kind that simply meets you where you are.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Embrace the ease of receiving therapy from the comfort of your own home with our online therapy sessions at Michelle Barratt Psychology. Our secure virtual setting provides the flexibility to navigate holiday stress while ensuring your privacy remains paramount.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Whether you’re facing family gatherings or just need a quiet moment of reflection, our convenient online sessions are here to support you. Book a session today and discover the ease of caring for your mental health, without leaving home.</p></div></section><section class="bg-blush "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold mb-8">More articles</h2><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">23 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising PTSD Counselling Needs in Toowong Adults</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Post-traumatic stress disorder, or PTSD, is not only something that happens to people in movies or in extreme situations. It can grow quietly in everyday lif…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">16 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Online Therapy in Brisbane When You Can’t Find Local Support</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Trying to find a psychologist in Brisbane can feel exhausting. You search, you join waitlists, you juggle your calendar, and still there is no appointment th…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">9 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising Trauma Counselling Needs in Toowong Professionals</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">High-performing professionals in Toowong are often good at holding it together. Work is busy, the pressure is high, and most people tell themselves it is jus…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac " href="/therapy-services">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',a={title:e,description:t,html:s};export{a as default,t as description,s as html,e as title};
